{"content":"# Emitter sweep: ~20 new one-line emitters have no direct test

## 🔵 SUGGESTION: sweep-test the new emitters like the degrade test does

The controller gained 49 emitter methods, but only ~29 are invoked anywhere
in tests (goldens + the two degrade/floor tests). Never called:
`toolPendingBg`, `customMessageBg`, `thinkingText`, `mdLink`, `mdCode`,
`mdCodeBlock`, `mdQuote`, `mdQuoteBorder`, `mdHr`, `mdListBullet`, `link`,
`syntaxFunction`, `syntaxNumber`, `syntaxType`, `syntaxOperator`,
`pythonMode`, `statusLineGitDirty`, `statusLineSpend`, `statusLineStaged`,
`statusLineDirty`, `statusLineUntracked`, `statusLineOutput`,
`statusLineSubagents`.

They are trivial delegations, but they are the entire E1 surface the S2–S6
stories will code against, and the changed-line coverage ratchet pays for
each uncovered line. A compact loop mirrors the existing ansi256 degrade
test and pins all of them at once:

```dart
test('every new emitter honors the profile seam', () {
  final controller = FaThemeController.instance;
  controller.switchTo('ohmypi-dark');
  final emitters = <String, String Function(String)>{
    'mdLink': controller.mdLink, 'pythonMode': controller.pythonMode,
    'statusLineSubagents': controller.statusLineSubagents, // … etc
  };
  controller.profile = ColorProfile.ansi256;
  for (final (name, emit) in emitters.entries) {
    expect(emit('x'), matches(RegExp(r'\x1b\[38;5;\d+m')),
        reason: name);
  }
  controller.profile = null;
  for (final (name, emit) in emitters.entries) {
    expect(emit('x'), 'x', reason: name);
  }
});
```

(Floor/parity coverage of the underlying *fields* is already excellent —
this is only about the method seam.)
